    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d514">

                <pb facs="0739" n="719" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg719"/>

                <head>Mr. Burnley to Mr.
                        Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-10-03"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 3, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Since I had the honor of addressing you on
                    the 31st August and 28th ultimo, relative to the sloop Racer, captured off
                    Bull’s bay by the United States steamer Hope, I have seen Captain Russell at
                    this legation, who informs me that himself and crew were released, and his
                    ship’s papers returned to him.</p>
                <p>These papers, which I herewith enclose in original, show that the vessel was
                    registered at and owned by British subjects at Nassau.</p>
                <p>I further enclose the affidavits of Captain Russell, his mate and crew, which
                    tend to show that they were engaged on a legitimate voyage, in a neutral vessel,
                    with registry and clearance perfectly legal and correct, having no cargo, or
                    anything to excite even suspicion.</p>
                <p>The detention for thirty-one days of the captain and crew appears to me,
                    therefore, illegal, as no proceedings of any kind were taken before a prize
                    court, and I am of opinion that their claims for compensation are entitled to
                    consideration.</p>
                <p>I beg you to return to me the affidavits and papers.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with the highest consideration, sir, your most obedient,
                    humble servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. HUME BURNLEY.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>



















